  "plan": {
    "goal": "Size the PLINK binary .bed dataset for a GWAS cohort of 1802 samples and 7232555 variants, including per-chromosome file sizing.",
    "rationale": "The binary .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples per byte). Full dataset size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome size uses the same rule applied to one chromosome's variant count. The largest chromosome (950419 variants) is consistent with human chromosome 1, so the dataset spans the standard human complement of 25 chromosomes (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT), giving 25 per-chromosome files.",
